  "Question": "What is \\(\\dfrac{2}{25}\\) written as a decimal?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.008\\)",
    "B": "\\(0.08\\)",
    "C": "\\(0.8\\)",
    "D": "\\(1.25\\)",
    "E": "\\(12.5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "A denominator of \\(100\\) lets us read the fraction directly as a decimal. Since \\(25\\cdot4=100\\), multiply both the numerator and denominator by \\(4\\):\n\\[\n\\frac2{25}=\\frac{2\\cdot4}{25\\cdot4}\n=\\frac8{100}=0.08.\n\\]\nThe decimal is \\(\\boxed{0.08}\\), choice B.",
